# Environment files. GLOB, NOT TWO LITERAL NAMES -- the previous `.env.local`
# and `.env` pair ignored exactly two filenames and left every other variant
# Next.js loads committable in a PUBLIC repository: `.env.development.local`,
# `.env.production.local`, `.env.development`, `.env.production`, and any
# ad-hoc `.env.sandbox`. `.env.development.local` is the standard file for a
# local override and OUTRANKS `.env.local`, so it is the one a developer
# reaches for precisely when they are handling credentials they do not want in
# their main env file. `.env.example` is the tracked template and is exempted.
.env*
!.env.example
node_modules/
.next/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
services/ingestion/__pycache__/

# TypeScript incremental build cache (regenerated on build)
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python virtualenvs (env artifact, never versioned)
.venv/

# Claude Code: local per-developer settings + transient agent worktrees.
# Scoped intentionally — shared config (.claude/settings.json, commands/,
# agents/, hooks/) stays trackable.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
